# Obsidian CS Knowledge Base — Note Conventions

This vault belongs to Akash Singh. **Read `CONVENTIONS.md` in the vault root before
writing or converting any note.** It is the authoritative spec. This file is a summary.

## The Two-Layer Model (most important convention)

Knowledge is stored in two linked layers:

- **`Course/`** — source layer. One note per course module, in course order, named
  `Module NN - <Topic>.md`. Preserves the course exactly as taught: outline, the
  instructor's examples, live code, full problem walkthroughs, your questions.
  Tag `source/<course-name>`.
- **Concept folders** (`Principles/`, `Patterns/`, `Concepts/`, `Structures/`) —
  distilled, source-independent knowledge absorbing the course *and* all other sources.

**Anti-duplication rule:** if the same paragraph would appear in both, it belongs in the
concept note; the module note links to it. Use transclusion (`![[Note#Heading]]`) to
display content in two places without copying.

## Folder Roles

- `Principles/` — rules used to *judge* a design (SOLID, coupling). Link down to patterns.
- `Patterns/` — one per design pattern. Must include a **recognition signal** and a
  **"confused with"** section. Link up to principles.
- `Problems/` — **only** designs solved independently with full knowledge. Course problem
  walkthroughs stay in their `Course/Module NN` note. Unsolved assignments go here with
  `status/todo`. A pattern taught inside a course problem still flows up to `Patterns/`.
- `Pattern Selection.md` — signal → pattern decision table plus commonly-confused pairs.
  Deliberately duplicates pattern notes; value is being one scannable page.

## Note Format

```
---
tags: [lld/patterns, status/draft]
created: YYYY-MM-DD
---
# Title
> [!abstract] One paragraph: what this is and why it matters
```

Callouts: `[!abstract]` open, `[!tip]` key insight, `[!warning]` gotcha, `[!danger]`
failure mode, `[!info]` context, `[!example]` worked example.

Diagrams: Mermaid first, `flowchart TD` default, `classDiagram` for LLD. Excalidraw only
when structure genuinely cannot be text. Node labels 2–4 words.

## Style

- `==highlight==` only for the single most critical fact on a line
- Complexity always in backticks: `O(log n)`
- Link concepts inline: "uses [[Strategy]] to swap payment methods"
- Every note ends with `## Related Notes` wikilinks
- No filler. Every line earns its place.

## Converting Handwritten Notes

User provides a PDF exported from OneNote (pages are images of freehand writing).
Read it, reconstruct as structured markdown per these conventions, recreate drawn
diagrams as Mermaid. One OneNote section = one `.md` file.
